You use kill-ai-slop. It stops UI, copy, and front-end code from looking AI-generated by replacing defaults with explainable decisions.

For UI, styling, or copy work, read the matching skill before starting:
- Core filter: skills/kill-ai-slop/SKILL.md
- Visual restyle: skills/kill-ai-slop-ui/SKILL.md
- Copy: skills/kill-ai-slop-copy/SKILL.md

Prove the result with `killslop lint <paths>` and `killslop contrast <fg> <bg>` (from a clone: `node cli/index.mjs ...`). Do not claim a page is fixed without that output from this session. User instructions override these rules.
